{
  "_comment": [
    "SetVectorPath (op 15) and VectorNode (shape 36). Run from BOTH sides:",
    "internal/core/golden_test.go and web/src/store/golden.test.ts.",
    "",
    "THE TWO SPACES (full rule in the proto, on `Anchor`): x/y are LOCAL to the",
    "node (the world point is Node.x + x, Node.y + y), in_/out_ are OFFSETS",
    "RELATIVE to the anchor. Here the numbers are chosen so that they READ that way:",
    "the offsets are small and centered on zero, not disguised coordinates.",
    "",
    "Four nodes, four cases:",
    " v1 -- creation + wholesale replacement. The two final subpaths have the",
    "       SAME anchors and differ ONLY by `closed`: a side that",
    "       ignored that field would produce two identical outlines and would fail",
    "       here instead of on the user's canvas.",
    " v2 -- the final anchors have the SAME x/y as the initial ones and only the",
    "       bezier handles change: a side that copied the points discarding",
    "       in_/out_ (or derived them by mirroring from out_) would pass",
    "       every check on the coordinates and fail only here. The handles",
    "       are asymmetric on purpose.",
    " v3 -- EMPTY list: the path the user emptied is a legitimate state,",
    "       not an 'unspecified' to ignore. The node stays a vector.",
    " v4 -- the SENTINEL. A triangle of CORNER points only: in_/out_ do not",
    "       appear at all, because proto3's zero IS the handle",
    "       coincident with the anchor, i.e. 'no handle'. The node",
    "       starts curved and ends sharp, so a side that filled in the",
    "       missing handles (or kept the previous ones) fails. It is also",
    "       the 'absent field' case of the round-trip, and it stays in the expected output instead of",
    "       being overwritten by a later op."
  ],
